Hi all,

As our traditional launch date is Haloween, we're about 3 weeks away from this
year's Tournament start.  Now is the time we usually post this announcement,
and a request for folks to volunteer servers for the Tournament.

As you may know, we suffered multiple drive crashes this summer, which mean
we're re-writing pretty much the whole system this month.  And I'm soooo happy
about that.  ;-)

We have the Game server system from last year, our expanded Tournament patch to
NetHack itself is ready to go and enough of the Control server is re-built to
let us start hooking in the Game servers.  So we're ready to start accepting
volunteers to set up Game servers for this year's Tournament; player
registration will start at midnight on Halloween, as usual.

The new system is set up so volunteers create accounts on the web site and
manage their server info from there, rather than emailing it to us, so anyone
interested in setting up early to help us test should please go to
<http://nethack.dev.null/tournament/registration.shtml> and set up their
account.

Thanks all,
-robin

Server Requirements:

(Remember, before volunteering, that anyone with admin level access to a game
server box is not allowed to compete; so don't volunteer to host if you want to
be a contender):

	a multi-user 3.4.3 NetHack installation (thus, probably, a Unix of some sort;
the /dev/null server is an OpenBSD system)

	an installed copy of our game server kit (see
<http://nethack.dev.null/software/index.shtml>

	sufficient speed/disk/memory to support 2500 player accounts and 26 concurrent
players (ours used to be a P133 with 32M of memory and 5G of disk, and that
should be plenty)

	a dedicated Internet connection (ours is on a T1; cable modems and DSL will
work fine, but it's dificult to do unless you have static IP numbers)

	since NetHack needs real user accounts, we'd recommend that it be a dedicated
system (the players will need to be entered in /etc/passwd to play on the box)


